WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.4 · Theory of Change
Activities

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Activities are the actions you and your co-founders will take to produce outputs.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Activities are the actions you, your co-founders and any partners will take to produce your outputs. Each one starts with a verb and is detailed enough to estimate the work and assign it.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Three checks for each activity

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:38.981
Starts with a verb: Clear enough to estimate the work and give it to someone. For example: Agree a referral route with the youth centre by March and train two mentors.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:50.681
Linked to an output: Every activity supports an output; if not, add the output or drop the activity. For example: “Visit local cafés” supports “two cafés and one canteen buying bread every week”.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:02.841
Feasible and acceptable: Timing, language, cost and local custom let people take part. For example: A trial shift shows trainees cannot arrive by 5 am, so shifts start at 7.

8
00:01:03.241 --> 00:01:03.841
Work that is easy to forget

9
00:01:03.841 --> 00:01:09.515
Preparation: booking the shared kitchen and agreeing who holds the key.

10
00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:14.819
Food-hygiene registration and the market-stall permit before the first Saturday.

11
00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:21.493
Safeguarding, mentoring and a check-in with each trainee after every shift.

12
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:22.493
Why they matter

13
00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:27.796
1. Clear activities let you plan and share out the work.

14
00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:32.730
2. Linking them to outputs cuts work that leads nowhere.

15
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:38.663
3. Checking feasibility early prevents a launch nobody can attend.

16
00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:39.663
What they guide

17
00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:43.856
1. Your inputs: the resources each activity needs.

18
00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:48.789
2. Your first plan and budget, in the Protect course.

19
00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:53.981
3. Roles for co-founders and tasks for volunteers.

20
00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:54.981
What to avoid

21
00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:58.433
Activities that support no output.

22
00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:02.256
Forgetting preparation, permissions, safeguarding and follow-up.

23
00:02:02.256 --> 00:02:07.819
Fixing dates before checking with the people involved.

24
00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:10.219
You list your main activities and the output each supports.

25
00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:14.219
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

26
00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:18.819
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
